elaine: Quick question — I merged a small change in chart values for webapp to prefer an ExternalSecret when present, PR: <https://git.redwood.example/org/webapp/pull/4522>. Helm lint and template in CI passed but in staging the pod starts without the envFrom mounting the secret. Any obvious templating guard I missed?

marco: can you paste the values you fed the helm release (or the snippet from the chart)? common mistake is the guard around .Values.externalSecret.name being an empty string vs nil.

elaine: values used in staging: `externalSecret: { enabled: true, name: "" }` — we purposely set name to empty in some overlays. Chart template currently:```yaml
{{- if .Values.externalSecret.enabled }}
envFrom:
  - secretRef:
      name: {{ .Values.externalSecret.name }}
{{- end }}
```

marco: ah, that's it. If name == "" Helm will still render `name: ` which results in a nil ref at runtime. You want to guard for non-empty name too. e.g.:```gotemplate
{{- $es := .Values.externalSecret }}
{{- if and $es.enabled (not (empty $es.name)) }}
envFrom:
  - secretRef:
      name: {{ $es.name | quote }}
{{- end }}
```

tanvi: another option is to default the overlay to null instead of empty string so `(empty $es.name)` works the same, or use `required` in charts where name must exist. For optional case I prefer the explicit guard. Also watch out if you use `tpl` on the name (values might contain `{{ }}`), then run `helm template` locally to confirm final manifest.

infra-bot: helm-lint/webapp-chart — template job: succeeded, integration-deploy/staging: failed — pod webapp-5b8f6 currently Running but `env` block missing secret reference (exit code: 0). More details in CI logs: <https://ci.redwood.example/job/12345/console> :warning:

ken: fwiw we should add a quick unit test in chart tests (helm-unittest or simple helm template diff) to catch empty-string secret names. Also add a pipeline check that overlays don't set `externalSecret.name: ""` silently.

elaine: thanks all — I'll patch the template to use the `empty` guard and push a small lint rule to the pipeline. Will also update the staging overlay to use null for name.

marco: thanks — also consider adding a short comment in values.yaml explaining empty string vs null behaviour so future PRs don't reintroduce this. :thumbsup:

elaine: will do, sending a follow-up PR in a bit.
